  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT085: Antae Base Left'
  blockDescription: This fragment bears the same scotia-torus-scotia molding as the
    column base, except in a rectalinear arrangement with bilateral symmetry. Thus
    it is identified as an "anta base", the base to one of the two piers terminating
    the lateral walls of the cella.
  blockPlacement: The fragment was found in the northwest side of the temple, and
    thus it is restored on the left anta of the temple.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ac80935bcad77154ca237d5e97bdaab2, type: 3}
