  blockTitle: 'AT175: Upper Column Drum'
  blockDescription: This fragment showcases a resting surface with a dowel hole,
    and a smaller diameter at the top with necking. These identify the fragment as
    the upper drum of one of the four unfluted columns, where the capital would be
    resting.
  blockPlacement: This column drum was found to the southeast of the temple and is
    restored at the rightmost column.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8aa612f73646c814caf1f2e5f355817e, type: 3}
