  blockTitle: 'AT203: Geison'
  blockDescription: This block is part of the highly decorated geison. It bears cuttings
    on the upper surface for the rafters of the roof, fake lionhead watersprouts
    on the overhang, and modilions and sculptural cassettes with floral and marine
    motifs in the overhand.
  blockPlacement: Found 12m. From the southwest side of the temple, it is restored
    as part of the horizontal geison on the right flank of the temple.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
