  descriptionText: {fileID: 6213780209972709613}
  placementText: {fileID: 8773322589981808993}
  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT 178: Front Pediment Tympanon (S)'
  blockDescription: "This is the central pediment tympanon block of the front fa\xE7ade.
    It bears sculptural decoration with a male bust in a wreath in the center, held
    by two flying Victories. The male figure bears the cone-capped quiver and the
    bow, characteristic features of Apollo, a god whom Emperor Caracalla appealed
    to for healing, and who appears in coinage minted during the same period."
  blockPlacement: "The pediment block was found at the southwest of the temple, and
    is restored at the front fa\xE7ade of the temple. "
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
