  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT194: Pediment Geison'
  blockDescription: Corner geison block with a raking profile of a geison drip (fascia,
    ovolo, fascia, ovolo, and cyma recta). Its underside has alternating modillions
    and floral motifs in the cassettes. It bears cuttings for the rafters of the
    roof and a flat support for an acroterion.
  blockPlacement: It was found to the southwest of the temple, and thus is restored
    at the right front corner of the temple.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d61330c6979e2284b8820f2f5b0b7216, type: 3}
