  blockDescription: This block is part of the horizontal geison block. It bears cuttings
    for the rafters of the roof on the upper surface, lion-head water spouts on the
    overhang, and modillions and cassettes with iconographic motifs (a turtle and
    an axe) in its underside.
  blockPlacement: Found 12m from the southwest side of the temple, it is restored
    as part of the horizontal geison on the right flank of the temple.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
