  descriptionText: {fileID: 6213780209972709613}
  placementText: {fileID: 8773322589981808993}
  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT429: Frieze'
  blockDescription: Freeze block that included a cyma profile and a dentil course
    on one of its long faces. However, it differs from other frieze blocks of the
    temple in that it is missing the taenia on top of the dentils, which would have
    made them more vulnerable to fractures during the installation and also would
    have reduced the overall height of the block.
  blockPlacement: This frieze block was found at the northeast of the temple, and
    it was probably the first frieze block from the back corner on the north flank
    of the temple.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
