  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT258: Pilaster Capital Right'
  blockDescription: 'This capital has two diagonally arranged faces with corinthian
    acanthus leaves in three rows: two at the bottom, three in the middle and two
    at the top, from which spring two tendrils, one towards the middle and one to
    the corner. It is a pilaster capital at the rear corner of the temple.'
  blockPlacement: It was found in the southeast side of the temple, close to its
    rear right corner, and thus it is restored there.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
