  displayDrawing1: {fileID: 2037472510}
  blockTitle: 'AT421: Architrave'
  blockDescription: This block has three fasciae of increasing height crowned by
    a simple ovolo and cavetto on two joining faces, consistent with the architrave
    of the temple. It's short length shows that it was on top of the cella wall and
    not spanning columns.
  blockPlacement: 'Found at the northeast side of the temple, and given it''s a corner
    block of short length, it is restored at the rear left corner of temple. '
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
