  blockDescription: These two fragments form a base that bears the scotia-torus-scotia
    molding like the column base. This base is rectalinear, has bilateral symmetry
    on the diagonal axis, and  is identified as one of the two pilaster bases at
    the rear corners of the temple.
  blockPlacement: Found at the northeast side of the temple, this base is restored
    at the left rear pilaster of the temple.
